d routes"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011CNExTxpq37QApTQAKjP6r","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java; grep -n \"specification.path\" build.gradle* ; ls ../ | head -30; grep -rln -i \"not found\\|404\\|no-such\" ../dca-ecommerce-specification 2>/dev/null | head","description":"Find the shared specification location"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":23,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the plan for CAT-03 to `tasks/CAT-03/plan.md`. The story is marked `adopted` (the shop already does this), so the plan changes no production code and no existing test.\n\n**Where the behaviour lives:**\n- When the product lookup finds nothing, the product page controller shows the `error/404` template (`ProductPageController.java:88-92`).\n- That template has the \"404\" code, the \"Page Not Found\" heading, the message and both links (`error/404.pug:5-12`).\n- The not-found branch sets no page title, so the shared layout falls back to \"domaincentric.commerce\" (`layout.pug:7`).\n- The links go to `/products`, headed \"Our Products\", and `/`, headed \"Welcome to domaincentric.commerce\".\n\n**Test levels:**\n- `unknown-product-shows-the-not-found-page` is the happy path, so it gets a Playwright browser test.\n- The other three scenarios get integration tests through the wired application.\n\n**No test covers any of the four scenarios yet.** Nearby tests only check the same destination pages when reached another way. No existing test contradicts the story, so the plan has no \"Changed tests\" section and needed no decision record.\n\n**Open assumptions a later stage should know:**\n- The not-found page returns HTTP 200, not 404. The story doesn't ask about the status, so nothing is planned for it.\n- Only the two links have `data-test` attributes. The code, heading and message would need them added if a test targets them directly.\n- Browser test names must match titles in a shared scenario catalogue outside this repository. That catalogue may not have one for this scenario yet; I didn't read it.\n\nI proposed one glossary term, \"Not-found page\". I didn't run the build or any other stage.","ttft_ms":2892,"type":"result","duration_ms":111996,"uuid":"f53012a0-a4b1-4ae3-a218-1c8541532884","ttft_stream_ms":1676,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":1676,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
